      "name": "Osu Kannon",
      "description": "Osu Kannon (formally Shinpukuji Hoshoin), a Shingon Chizan-sect temple in Nagoya's Osu district, moved to its present site in 1612. Its library, the Osu Bunko, holds about 15,000 volumes including a National Treasure manuscript of the Kojiki, and an antique market opens on the 18th and 28th of each month.",
      "highlights": ["History"]
    },
    "ja": {
      "name": "大須観音",
      "description": "大須観音（正式名称・北野山真福寺宝生院）。真言宗智山派の寺院で、1612年に現在地へ移転した。大須文庫には国宝の古事記写本など約15,000冊を収蔵し、毎月18日・28日の縁日には骨董市が立つ。",
      "highlights": ["歴史"]
